[{"id":"VRCE-2-86-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":1,"english":"Having passed that night, Bharata having been entertained along with his family, appeared before Bharadvāja, desirous (of seeing Rāma).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24b28289c874dcaeed15d1fa201428463b047ad3563ed2a4408980478d0cec91","compact":"210594341a3f57e4bfc87f05976b1e32aa7b605ef4cd872faf4d17f4a5cbd53a","nasal":"210594341a3f57e4bfc87f05976b1e32aa7b605ef4cd872faf4d17f4a5cbd53a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":2,"english":"Seeing that foremost of men (standing) with joined hands, Bharadvāja, who had just finished his fire-sacrifice, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29cdbeb53b82d494048c8e5b941ddd043c82ca8706a590331ff1d2b759836240","compact":"2c001c3ae62e52eeb6a34ad192f6b52908b7d379ee2a9a1d6b1b05a9d7039803","nasal":"f90e10c4c2591ae48ab5c30f86514ed63b80d3e3e85d043e30d1ad52e8a033a0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":3,"english":"Have you passed the night pleasantly at our place? And have all your men been pleased with our hospitality? Do you tell me this O sinless one. we","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5be510f50a78c438a91b1d71bba4dae85443516898e51fcbc3603098660f5890","compact":"febe3d1fa31e32cac9049d8d41e4a7eacc11206f8f8c39c796d5f738e461c6ff","nasal":"febe3d1fa31e32cac9049d8d41e4a7eacc11206f8f8c39c796d5f738e461c6ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":4,"english":"Thereupon, Bharata bowing down, with joined hands said to that ascetic of excellent energy, as he had issued out of his hermitage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9479fa44dae75263c9893c43567bc2c4723e9ea854e367ea6ad0f0cd2b12d187","compact":"9d23d80e3b23d2ce29bb922d8a8dd4f745b049a96969193b4cfee542e71e2f6e","nasal":"775ca93fbda70fb53e5d908f3726e7985b9112695fee3af1449644fad7bf34bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":5,"english":"O reverend Sire, I along with all my forces and vehicles have passed (the night) happily. I have been full well entertained by you, o worshipful one possessed of power. And with our languor and heat removed, all sumptuously feasted and comfortably quartered, have passed (the night) agreeably along with our servants.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.379,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e48dcbc706fe1712ad658f070f34141a7f88bd66c6d2ea8886ae64eb5d74177","compact":"223af9fbaeb1250c8f7547468f2d495b73ca545c6140f95571670ea72e7074da","nasal":"223af9fbaeb1250c8f7547468f2d495b73ca545c6140f95571670ea72e7074da"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":6,"english":"O reverend Sire, I along with all my forces and vehicles have passed (the night) happily. I have been full well entertained by you, o worshipful one possessed of power. And with our languor and heat removed, all sumptuously feasted and comfortably quartered, have passed (the night) agreeably along with our servants.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5389c40a2e3c39d2e9f3905db8e938aa78524e2306114c673189bb4d072ef12b","compact":"6420caee15f70263c05ed364d1142c9ac93f49557e242833874a9585ca4868b2","nasal":"6420caee15f70263c05ed364d1142c9ac93f49557e242833874a9585ca4868b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":7,"english":"Now, O best of ascetics, I beseech you to look with a propitious eye on me who am bound for my brother's place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4a3a345e9d0716845f7a9d1648d55d75fae01ec83052b9308642e3f63b6cd1e","compact":"fbaa06010e0dd1639c0dfc4516cd5dbc8e1b1073be34b45ff96c6eb60036cce1","nasal":"27ee660ddcc1d46b75f0899ee11b0f6ea6487ac43e86241e7638719a401b9220"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":8,"english":"And tell me, O you cognizant of morality, how far is it to that high-souled righteous one's asylm, and by what way (shall I reach there)?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22111e62c641df7828ec446e769e599e0f7773a761878da806bc82d20397078b","compact":"c214b751b03bd9478d95219b9c2e4fc059f65bb2260ea0c191ed2d1dab6fa589","nasal":"c214b751b03bd9478d95219b9c2e4fc059f65bb2260ea0c191ed2d1dab6fa589"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":9,"english":"When Bharata eager to see his brother had asked thus, the highly energetic Bharadvāja of rigid austerities answered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92a5056a9b1bd43dc8bb5ecc83a44b35d0a81d04dff8ce812d31a81079935043","compact":"631f9e27cf05c9726e098cb9cc840db0a3198dfe5a3d6a22068b4e21cdbf4899","nasal":"d4f10cdad9ed6e42b60375df6bae4754cc69477001f4860f5ff8f5b5ac1f5a0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":10,"english":"O Bharata, two and a half Yojanas hence, embossed in a tenantless wood is the mountain Citrakuta, charming with rocks and woods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.732,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24e8dc1d2f848b0f93f66c30416de9282b87dd62554fd76100396f8c5a1672e3","compact":"5f4d0329d152bf3b2f450d674ec70dd0ce13accb32f058af042934d1840036e4","nasal":"5f4d0329d152bf3b2f450d674ec70dd0ce13accb32f058af042934d1840036e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":11,"english":"On its northern border flows the river Mandākinſ, covered with flowering trees and with blossoming woods. Beyond the stream is the mountain Citrakuta. There is their thatched cottage, my child; there they abide for certain.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"381cf0abfe3e069ed2a703747e6bf5470163ccfab9437e15fca62acbfb62