alue; and the infantry went on foot.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74ae4cf67d7a980b092e6d4394cda8a1ead7f098f6ba0e5fbe71653d6197a1bc","compact":"cc48aeef57bffc34c85dd5663ac0bb2fcb161b248369e44e796798711ba68bf9","nasal":"cc48aeef57bffc34c85dd5663ac0bb2fcb161b248369e44e796798711ba68bf9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":33,"english":"And on a magnificent car went the ladies headed by Kausalyā, with delighted hearts, eager to see Rāghava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de833a08352c2a9b9a58c66a4777a671b074b699e1d0992f8b7265741f0ac293","compact":"39970436bfc59e1e9afb2a04cd23c61c2e8fa987e755af9b864555f7d16dddff","nasal":"b904fb31675f23da308e9531030b657bdb48748661d4e9683a3610dbaaf789fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":34,"english":"And ascending an elegant car resembling the infant sun or moon, driven by charioteers, went the graceful Bharata well attired.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.969,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-92-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2086034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c9924d193e9e5be1dfe8ddf65948580b5e1175acb0171fb7003f8604b4f4ab94","compact":"2e321cbaf4ea175aff77a17fb8a6b4c43157044b7b864555b85c22441369477b","nasal":"2e321cbaf4ea175aff77a17fb8a6b4c43157044b7b864555b85c22441369477b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-86-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":86,"verse":35,"english":"And that might